Title: Everyone Here Is Happy
Credit: Halloween short, based on the story by
Author: Josh
Draft date: October 31, 2026
Notes: Three minutes, first person throughout (we are Dad; we see only his hands). 9:16. No Manager voice. Shot numbers in [[ ]] match the shot list in D:\Comfy\blockout-previs-demo\halloween-playways\SHOT_LIST.md.

INT. HAPPY HANK'S PIZZA & PLAY - PARTY ROOM - DAY

/* The venue and mascot names are placeholders: an original knock-off brand. */

[[S01]] Our POV, seated. Two hands around a paper coffee cup. Fluorescent light. A birthday table of shrieking four-year-olds, a lopsided sheet cake, a game room blinking beyond.

[[S02]] A paper crown drops over our eyes. Darkness and a gold paper edge.

Our hand lifts it.

SARAH, four, blue top, a yellow plastic star on her left wrist, kneels on the seat beside us. She adjusts the crown. Worse.

[[S03]] She laughs. She slides down and taps the table edge twice.

SARAH
You say ready.

[[S04]] Our hand takes the crown off and sets it on the table.

DAD (O.S.)
Ready.

Sarah hops over a colored line in the carpet. Turns to check we saw.

[[S05]] Across the room, the MASCOT, a cheap orange costume with a too-wide grin, waves at a table of kids. Its head turns toward us. It waves at us too. The smile does not change.

[[S06]] On the table, our phone buzzes.

INSERT - PHONE

LENA: Mark and I can grab her if you're not up to it.

[[S07]] Our thumb starts a reply. Stops. Deletes.

[[S08]] We look up. Sarah is at the ball-pit rail, waving both arms.

SARAH
Dad. Watch this one.

DAD (O.S.)
One second.

[[S09]] Back down to the phone. Up again. Sarah climbs into the pit.

INT. PARTY ROOM - BALL PIT - CONTINUOUS

[[S10]] Sarah wades to a foam step. A BIGGER KID gets there first and shoves her. She falls back into the balls.

[[S11]] Her cry cuts through the party. We put the phone face down and stand.

[[S12]] We cross the room fast, weaving between tables.

DAD (O.S.)
Hey. Hey, I'm here.

[[S13]] Sarah scrambles out of the pit, crying, and runs along the rail into the mouth of the play structure. Gone.

[[S14]] We crouch at the structure entrance. A padded tube runs into the dark. Her sneakers vanish around the bend.

INT. PLAY STRUCTURE - CONTINUOUS

[[S15]] We crawl. Our hands slap padded vinyl. The party is loud behind us.

DAD (O.S.)
Sarah?

[[S16]] A net tunnel. Far ahead, a flash of blue top turning a corner.

[[S17]] A junction. Three tubes. We take the one she must have taken.

[[S18]] Something yellow on the tube floor. Her star. Our hand picks it up. We pocket it.

[[S19]] A long straight tube. Longer than the building. The party noise thins to nothing but a hum.

[[S20]] A junction. The same peeling sticker on the same panel. We have been here.

[[S21]] Padded steps leading down. The light turns warmer. Dimmer.

[[S22]] A slide mouth we did not see before. Dark inside. Air moving out of it.

DAD (O.S.)
(quiet)
Sarah?

[[S23]] We climb in. The floor tips. We slide.

[[S24]] Faster. Spiraling. Light strobes through the translucent tube walls.

[[S25]] It keeps going. Far longer than any slide. A disc of light at the end, growing.

INT. THE PLAYWAYS - THE BASIN

[[S26]] We shoot out of the tube into open air. Below: a sea of balls, rushing up.

[[S27]] Under. Colored dark. Muffled. Our hands claw.

[[S28]] Our hands break the surface. We gasp. Silence where the party was. A low hum.

[[S29]] We look up.

A tower of tubes, net bridges, and lit windows rises out of the haze, and keeps rising.

[[S30]] We wade to the edge of the pit and haul ourselves onto a padded ledge.

[[S31]] Far off, on a net bridge: a small figure in a blue top. Back turned.

DAD (O.S.)
Sarah!

[[S32]] We move toward her. To the left, in a lit window: another small figure in a blue top. On a slide below it: another.

[[S33]] We turn. On every bridge, a child in a blue top. Back turned.

[[S34]] We look up. Every tier, every window, every tube, rising into the haze: small figures in blue tops, all facing away.

Above them, the MASCOT, a hundred feet tall, grins down. It does not move.

[[S35]] We look down at the yellow star in our hand.

[[S36]] We look up into the tower. It has no top.

CUT TO BLACK.

EVERYONE HERE IS HAPPY

END
